/-!
# Candidate seed cosets for finite extension certificates

The rows give thirty-two actual Sylow normal forms for each seed. There are
only twenty-three different lists. Their definition asserts neither coset
coverage nor a seed order. The independent factorization certificate must
express every Sylow normal form as a seed element times a listed representative.

Together with the existing eighteen Sylow double cosets, these candidates give
literal elements `t * r * u⁻¹` for testing single-element extensions. Left and
right multiplication by elements of the seed preserve the generated extension.

Source: the Parrott (1972), section 5, p.683 marking, the existing normal forms,
and the reproducible, untrusted discovery in `source/` beside this module.
-/

@[expose] public section
